## 2. Earned Value Management (EVM)

### 2.1 Assumptions

- **Budget at Completion (BAC):** $1,150,000, the approved budget in the Project Scope Statement.
- **Total scope:** 89 story points (Sprint 1: 32, Sprint 2: 29, Sprint 3: 28). The deferred Curbside Geo-Arrival Tracking items are excluded per the CCB decision.
- **Project length:** The project is 3 sprints long, so through the end of Sprint 2, 2/3 of the budget is the Planned Value (PV) and 2/3 of the budget is the Actual Cost (AC), per the assignment instructions.
- **Earned Value (EV):** Completed story points ÷ total story points × BAC. Through Sprint 2, 61 of 89 points are complete (68.5%).
- Because PV and AC are set to the same value under these assumptions, SPI and CPI are numerically identical. This is expected and not a calculation error.

### 2.2 Baseline Metrics Through Sprint 2

| Metric | Formula | Calculation | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Planned Value (PV)** | 2/3 × BAC | 2/3 × $1,150,000 | **$766,667** |
| **Earned Value (EV)** | (Points done ÷ Total points) × BAC | (61 ÷ 89) × $1,150,000 | **$788,202** |
| **Actual Cost (AC)** | 2/3 × BAC | 2/3 × $1,150,000 | **$766,667** |
| **Schedule Variance (SV)** | EV − PV | $788,202 − $766,667 | **+$21,535** |
| **Cost Variance (CV)** | EV − AC | $788,202 − $766,667 | **+$21,535** |
| **Schedule Performance Index (SPI)** | EV ÷ PV | $788,202 ÷ $766,667 | **1.03** |
| **Cost Performance Index (CPI)** | EV ÷ AC | $788,202 ÷ $766,667 | **1.03** |

### 2.3 Interpretation

- **SPI = 1.03:** The project is about 3% ahead of schedule. The team completed 61 points against a planned 59.3 points (2/3 of 89), which is roughly 1.7 points ahead.
- **CPI = 1.03:** The project is about 3% more cost-efficient than planned. Each dollar spent has produced about $1.03 of planned value.
- **Variances:** Both SV and CV are positive ($21,535), so the project is ahead of schedule and under budget.
- **Health:** Green. Both indices are above 1.0, and all committed work in Sprints 1 and 2 was completed with no carryover.

### 2.4 Sprint 3 Forecast

| Metric | Formula | Calculation | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Estimate at Completion (EAC)** | BAC ÷ CPI | $1,150,000 ÷ 1.0281 | **$1,118,580** |
| **Estimate to Complete (ETC)** | EAC − AC | $1,118,580 − $766,667 | **$351,913** |
| **Variance at Completion (VAC)** | BAC − EAC | $1,150,000 − $1,118,580 | **+$31,420** |

**Forecast narrative:** If the team keeps its current cost efficiency (CPI of 1.03), the project is forecast to finish at about $1.119M, roughly $31,420 (2.7%) under the approved budget. The remaining 28 story points sit in Sprint 3 (Nov 09 to Nov 22), which is below the 30.5-point average velocity, so the team is on track to finish before the December 4, 2026 deadline.

**Risks to the forecast:**
- Sprint 3 includes UAT (#23) and pilot store onboarding (#22), which depend on stakeholder availability and store feedback that may require rework.
- Training work (16 of the 28 points) relies on store managers scheduling sessions without overtime, which is a scope statement assumption.
- If CPI fell to 0.95 in Sprint 3, EAC would rise to about $1.21M, so the project would exceed the $1,150,000 budget. Monitor cost closely during Sprint 3.
